  "difficulty_reason": "Counted unit: the article's Theorem 1 (source0.tex lines 724-735), the global convergence theorem of the accelerated proximal PRS-SQP algorithm with dual ascent-descent procedures: every accumulation point of the sequence generated by the algorithm is a Karush-Kuhn-Tucker point of the composite problem. The retained complete proof (lines 736-777) is a genuine 42-line argument, not a routine verification: it must combine the stationarity and feasibility estimates of the preceding lemmas, control the behaviour of the multipliers produced by the dual ascent-descent step through the boundedness and nondegeneracy lemmas, pass to a convergent subsequence using the proximity measure of the proximal step, and then verify the KKT conditions in the limit using the exact penalty term of the augmented Lagrangian. The residual difficulty is that convergence must be established without convexity of the composite model, through the interaction of three coupled sequences (primal, dual and penalty); this is research-level nonlinear programming well beyond ordinary PhD qualifying exercises.",
